\subsection{Ablation Studies}

To systematically validate each architectural component's contribution, we conduct comprehensive ablation experiments. Table~\ref{tab:ablation} presents ablation results analyzing: (1) incremental component addition starting from baseline concatenation fusion; (2) component removal from the full model to assess individual importance; (3) fusion strategy variants comparing cross-attention against alternatives; (4) architecture variants (CNN-only, Transformer-only, Hybrid).

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{Ablation study analyzing contributions of key components. Baseline: dual-path CNN with simple concatenation fusion.}
\label{tab:ablation}
\begin{tabular}{lccc}
\toprule
